From 414ccd66b572b1e470a7b5643940d4a84c1ca9f7 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: "Mohamed R. Khalil" <m.radwan.khalil@gmail.com>
Date: Tue, 20 Oct 2026 01:36:55 +0300
Subject: [PATCH] fix(background-agent): acknowledge parent wakes answered
 after a slow first token

Incident ses_eede11ad1ffe (2026-10-19): the wake was dispatched in 10 ms,
but the parent took 20.2 s to stream its first token. The 5 s recovery
window saw no output and requeued the wake. The answer then cleared only
the dispatched entry; the requeued pending wake re-dispatched as a noReply
admission and a reply retry, and the owner saw the completion twice.

- Recovery window: an assistant turn started after the dispatch that has
  not completed or failed extends the window (bounded to 5 min) instead
  of counting as "no output".
- Record replyDispatchedAt on the first accepted reply dispatch and keep
  it across requeues (reset when new notifications merge in). A requeued
  wake whose earlier dispatch was answered is dropped before any
  re-dispatch or deadline notice.
- Retry dedupe keys carry the reply mode, so a noReply admission can no
  longer coalesce away the reply dispatch of the same retry.
